  "_comment": "Button captions. Every one of these sends a request, and a good few write to a live vehicle, so they name the action rather than describing it: 'Write VIN', not 'VIN writing'. Recurring vocabulary: CPE = central door locking, EV = solenoid valve, RAZ (remise à zéro) = reset, MàF = firing line (airbag squib), APV = after-sales, GMP = powertrain, Verlog = software version, Lève-vitre = window lift, Essuyage = wipe, Conda/Condamnation = lock. Several source strings are typos in the database ('Ecirure', 'Ecritute') and are translated by intent. Repeated '...Arrêt...' variants differ only in leading dots, which the original used to space a row of buttons; each keeps its own entry so the layout is unchanged.",

